<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <!-- matches the core framework rather than CmdUi's net10.0: a terminal interface is
             useful to every tool the framework supports, and Spectre.Console targets
             netstandard2.0, so nothing here forces net10 -->
        <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <Title>Terminal user interface for Benday.CommandsFramework tools</Title>
        <Description>An in-process terminal UI for any tool built on Benday.CommandsFramework. Reference this package and call .WithTui() and the tool gains a 'tui' keyword that browses its commands, fills in a form and runs it without leaving the terminal.</Description>
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <Authors>benday</Authors>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/benday-inc/Benday.CommandsFramework</PackageProjectUrl>
        <Copyright>2026</Copyright>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/benday-inc/Benday.CommandsFramework.git</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageIcon>bdc_mark_128_128.png</PackageIcon>
        <PackageTags>dotnet;cli;command-line;tui;terminal;console;commands;framework</PackageTags>
        <TheVersion>5.1.0</TheVersion>
        <AssemblyVersion>$(TheVersion).0</AssemblyVersion>
        <Version>$(TheVersion)</Version>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>
v5.1 - First release. Adds the 'tui' keyword to any tool that references this package and calls .WithTui() on the CommandsApp builder; Browse the tool's commands grouped by category and nested by command group, with a fuzzy filter across names, aliases, categories and descriptions; Fill in a command's arguments in a form that picks its widget from the argument's own type, validates each value as it is typed without ever storing one the argument refuses, and reports what is wrong through the command's own validation; A live command line preview shows what the form adds up to, rendered in whichever argument syntax the tool accepts, with copy to clipboard; Running a command from the interface is not implemented yet;
        </PackageReleaseNotes>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="..\..\bdc_mark_128_128.png">
            <Pack>True</Pack>
            <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
        </None>
        <None Include="..\..\README.md">
            <Pack>True</Pack>
            <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
        </None>
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Spectre.Console" Version="0.57.2" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Benday.CommandsFramework\Benday.CommandsFramework.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
